# Copy to `pns_adb_device.env` (same folder, gitignored) and set your USB device serial from `adb devices`.
# Used when `-Serial` is omitted by scripts such as:
#   `pns_adb_preview_validate.ps1`, `pns_milestone6_gate.ps1`, `pns_sideload_and_launch.ps1`,
#   `pns_automation_smoke.ps1`, `pns_chrome_ux_gate.ps1`, `pns_fleet_matrix_scan.ps1`,
#   `pns_failure_matrix_smoke.ps1`, `pns_hfr_autorun.ps1` (`-PerfReport`), `pns_capture_perfetto_light.ps1`,
#   `pns_root_capability_adb.ps1`, `pns_device_screencap.ps1`, `pns_pull_dcim_captures.ps1`, and `pns_face_meter_probe.ps1`.
#
# If more than one device is online, set `PNS_ADB_SERIAL` or pass `-Serial <serial>` where supported.
#
# Primary fleet development device (Milestone 16.10): OnePlus 12 CPH2583
#   PNS_ADB_SERIAL=b5214fc6
# Wi‑Fi (same LAN as PC — often 10.0.0.x, not 10.1.10.x):
#   PNS_ADB_SERIAL=10.0.0.9:42219
#   PNS_ADB_PAIR_HOST_PORT=10.0.0.9:37123   # from "Pair device with pairing code" dialog only
#   PNS_ADB_PAIR_CODE=123456
# Helper: .\scripts\pns_adb_wifi_connect.ps1 -PairHostPort ... -PairCode ... -ConnectHostPort ...
# Optional: `adb mdns services` lists `_adb-tls-pairing._tcp` when pair dialog is open.
#
# Community ingest endpoint (Render):
LEADERBOARD_INGEST_URL=https://pns-leaderboard-ingest.onrender.com
#
# Optional legacy regression lane (local only — not the default proof device):
#   PNS_ADB_SERIAL=<legacy-device-serial>
#
# Optional notes for humans/agents (not parsed):
# PNS_ADB_ROOT_AVAILABLE=1
#
# Prefer Android SDK platform-tools on PATH (or dot-source pns_resolve_adb.ps1 -PrependToPath)
# so logcat/pull match Studio/Gradle — desktop adb copies can yield empty PNS.FleetMatrix logs.

PNS_ADB_SERIAL=
